<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peter Kenilorea</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1943–2016</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sir Peter Kenilorea was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a> Islands teacher and politician who became chief minister in 1976 and the first prime minister when the islands became independent from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> on 7 July 1978. He served as prime minister again in the mid-1980s and later as speaker of the national parliament.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peter-kenilorea.jpg" alt="Peter Kenilorea" width="320" height="390" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jenny Scott from Adelaide, Australia · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peter_Kenilorea_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
